{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-77677" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the line $y=2x-5$ and linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is the equation of the image of the line under the action of $T?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012907/state.json" "file_sha256" "7cd2bd93010edbee5b73a4ba8b26321926de8a3ce2424ca13ea442d8f5662cea"} {"question" "q-77677" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, notice that the line $y=2x-5$ passes through the points $A(0,-5)$ and $B(1,-3)$ since the coordinates of both points satisfy the equation.\n\nTo find the image of $A$ and $B$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing the coordinates of the points:\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -5 & -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -5 & -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective image points are ${A}^{′}(5,0)$ and ${B}^{′}(4,2).$\n\nFinally, we write the equation of the line that passes through ${A}^{′}$ and ${B}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}}(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-0 & =\\frac{2-0}{4-5}(x-5) \\\\ y & =-2(x-5) \\\\ y & =-2x+10 \\\\ 2x+y-10 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012907/state.json" "file_sha256" "7cd2bd93010edbee5b73a4ba8b26321926de8a3ce2424ca13ea442d8f5662cea"} {"question" "q-77677" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012907/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "202a2e0f4a0652e6263fb253f02cfef9dfd32dc8ec431618ecea2cf72c1a7fc2"} {"question" "q-77677" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012907/state.json" "file_sha256" "7cd2bd93010edbee5b73a4ba8b26321926de8a3ce2424ca13ea442d8f5662cea"} {"question" "q-77677" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2x+y-10=0"] ["math" "2x-y+10=0"] ["math" "2x-y-5=0"] ["math" "x+y-10=0"] ["math" "x+y-5=0"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012907/state.json" "file_sha256" "7cd2bd93010edbee5b73a4ba8b26321926de8a3ce2424ca13ea442d8f5662cea"} {"question" "q-77677" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2x+y-10=0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012907/state.json" "file_sha256" "7cd2bd93010edbee5b73a4ba8b26321926de8a3ce2424ca13ea442d8f5662cea"} {"question" "q-77776" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the line $y=4x-1$ and linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is the equation of the image of the line under the action of $T?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012907/state.json" "file_sha256" "7cd2bd93010edbee5b73a4ba8b26321926de8a3ce2424ca13ea442d8f5662cea"} {"question" "q-77776" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, notice that the line $y=4x-1$ passes through the points $Q(0,-1)$ and $R(1,3)$ since the coordinates of both points satisfy the equation.\n\nTo find the image of $Q$ and $R$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing the coordinates of the points:\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -10 \\\\ -2 & 6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective image points are ${Q}^{′}(3,-2)$ and ${R}^{′}(-10,6).$\n\nFinally, we write the equation of the line that passes through ${Q}^{′}$ and ${R}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}}(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-(-2) & =\\frac{6-(-2)}{-10-3}(x-3) \\\\ y+2 & =-\\frac{8}{13}(x-3) \\\\ 13y+26 & =-8x+24 \\\\ 8x+13y+2 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012907/state.json" "file_sha256" "7cd2bd93010edbee5b73a4ba8b26321926de8a3ce2424ca13ea442d8f5662cea"} {"question" "q-77776" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012907/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "202a2e0f4a0652e6263fb253f02cfef9dfd32dc8ec431618ecea2cf72c1a7fc2"} {"question" "q-77776" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012907/state.json" "file_sha256" "7cd2bd93010edbee5b73a4ba8b26321926de8a3ce2424ca13ea442d8f5662cea"} {"question" "q-77776" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "13x+3y+2=0"] ["math" "13x+8y+2=0"] ["math" "8x+13y+2=0"] ["math" "8x+3y+12=0"] ["math" "8x+3y+2=0"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012907/state.json" "file_sha256" "7cd2bd93010edbee5b73a4ba8b26321926de8a3ce2424ca13ea442d8f5662cea"} {"question" "q-77776" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "8x+13y+2=0"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012907/state.json" "file_sha256" "7cd2bd93010edbee5b73a4ba8b26321926de8a3ce2424ca13ea442d8f5662cea"} {"question" "q-77794" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the line $x=1$ and linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is the equation of the image of the line under the action of $T?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012907/state.json" "file_sha256" "7cd2bd93010edbee5b73a4ba8b26321926de8a3ce2424ca13ea442d8f5662cea"} {"question" "q-77794" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, notice that the line $x=1$ passes through the points $J(1,0)$ and $K(1,1)$ since the coordinates of both points satisfy the equation.\n\nTo find the image of $J$ and $K$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing the coordinates of the points:\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective image points are ${J}^{′}(2,1)$ and ${K}^{′}(0,4).$\n\nFinally, we write the equation of the line that passes through ${J}^{′}$ and ${K}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}}(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-1 & =\\frac{4-1}{0-2}(x-2) \\\\ y-1 & =-\\frac{3}{2}(x-2) \\\\ 2y-2 & =-3x+6 \\\\ 3x+2y-8 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012907/state.json" "file_sha256" "7cd2bd93010edbee5b73a4ba8b26321926de8a3ce2424ca13ea442d8f5662cea"} {"question" "q-77794" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012907/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "202a2e0f4a0652e6263fb253f02cfef9dfd32dc8ec431618ecea2cf72c1a7fc2"} {"question" "q-77794" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012907/state.json" "file_sha256" "7cd2bd93010edbee5b73a4ba8b26321926de8a3ce2424ca13ea442d8f5662cea"} {"question" "q-77794" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2x+y+5=0"] ["math" "2x+y-2=0"] ["math" "3x+2y-8=0"] ["math" "4x+y-5=0"] ["math" "4x-y+5=0"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012907/state.json" "file_sha256" "7cd2bd93010edbee5b73a4ba8b26321926de8a3ce2424ca13ea442d8f5662cea"} {"question" "q-77794" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3x+2y-8=0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012907/state.json" "file_sha256" "7cd2bd93010edbee5b73a4ba8b26321926de8a3ce2424ca13ea442d8f5662cea"} {"question" "q-278618" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the line $y=3x+5$ and linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn **standard form**, the equation of the image of the line under the action of $T$ is\n\n{{field-1}}$=-40.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012907/state.json" "file_sha256" "7cd2bd93010edbee5b73a4ba8b26321926de8a3ce2424ca13ea442d8f5662cea"} {"question" "q-278618" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, notice that the line $y=3x+5$ passes through the points $A(0,5)$ and $B(1,8)$ since the coordinates of both points satisfy the equation.\n\nTo find the image of $A$ and $B$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing the coordinates of the points:\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 8\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-10 & -16 \\\\ 5 & 12\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective image points are ${A}^{′}(-10,5)$ and ${B}^{′}(-16,12).$\n\nNow, we write the equation of the line that passes through ${A}^{′}$ and ${B}^{′}$ in point-slope form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}}(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-5 & =\\frac{12-5}{-16-(-10)}(x-(-10)) \\\\ y-5 & =-\\frac{7}{6}(x+10)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we transform the equation of the line to standard form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-5 & =-\\frac{7}{6}(x+10) \\\\ 6y-30 & =-7x-70 \\\\ 7x+6y & =-40\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012907/state.json" "file_sha256" "7cd2bd93010edbee5b73a4ba8b26321926de8a3ce2424ca13ea442d8f5662cea"} {"question" "q-278618" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012907/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "202a2e0f4a0652e6263fb253f02cfef9dfd32dc8ec431618ecea2cf72c1a7fc2"} {"question" "q-278618" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012907/state.json" "file_sha256" "7cd2bd93010edbee5b73a4ba8b26321926de8a3ce2424ca13ea442d8f5662cea"} {"question" "q-278618" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "7x+6y"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012907/state.json" "file_sha256" "7cd2bd93010edbee5b73a4ba8b26321926de8a3ce2424ca13ea442d8f5662cea"} {"question" "q-281578" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the line $x=4$ and linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn **standard form**, the equation of the image of the line under the action of $T$ is\n\n{{field-1}}$=16.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012907/state.json" "file_sha256" "7cd2bd93010edbee5b73a4ba8b26321926de8a3ce2424ca13ea442d8f5662cea"} {"question" "q-281578" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, notice that the line $x=4$ passes through the points $G(4,0)$ and $H(4,1)$ since the coordinates of both points satisfy the equation.\n\nTo find the image of $G$ and $H$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing the coordinates of the points:\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}12 & 10 \\\\ 4 & 6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective image points are ${G}^{′}(12,4)$ and ${H}^{′}(10,6).$\n\nNow, we write the equation of the line that passes through ${G}^{′}$ and ${H}^{′}$ in point-slope form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}}(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-4 & =\\frac{6-4}{10-12}(x-12) \\\\ y-4 & =-1(x-12)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we transform the equation of the line to standard form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-4 & =-x+12 \\\\ x+y & =16\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012907/state.json" "file_sha256" "7cd2bd93010edbee5b73a4ba8b26321926de8a3ce2424ca13ea442d8f5662cea"} {"question" "q-281578" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012907/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "202a2e0f4a0652e6263fb253f02cfef9dfd32dc8ec431618ecea2cf72c1a7fc2"} {"question" "q-281578" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012907/state.json" "file_sha256" "7cd2bd93010edbee5b73a4ba8b26321926de8a3ce2424ca13ea442d8f5662cea"} {"question" "q-281578" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x+y"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14012907/state.json" "file_sha256" "7cd2bd93010edbee5b73a4ba8b26321926de8a3ce2424ca13ea442d8f5662cea"}] "usage" {"q-77677" []} "basis" 1162 "retractions" [[17592186152694 :question/problem "Consider the line $y = 2x - 5$ and linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T$, given by\n\n$T = \\beg